``` The same three detections as detect.py, written as Splunk searches (SPL).
    Run each search separately with the time range set to "All time".
    Every search starts by extracting the fields from the raw log line:
    2026-08-30 16:39:45 | user=rpatel | ip=203.0.113.45 | event=login_success | status=success | location=Chicago,US ```


``` 1. Brute force (MITRE T1110): more than 5 failed logins from one IP inside a 10-minute sliding window.
    streamstats with time_window is the SPL version of the two-pointer sliding window in detect_brute_force(). ```
index=main sourcetype=auth_log
| rex "user=(?<user>\S+) \| ip=(?<src_ip>\S+) \| event=(?<event>\S+) \| status=(?<result>\S+) \| location=(?<city>[^,]+),(?<country>\S+)"
| search result=failure
| sort 0 _time
| streamstats time_window=10m count AS failures_in_window BY src_ip
| where failures_in_window > 5
| stats max(failures_in_window) AS max_failures, values(user) AS targeted_users, min(_time) AS first_seen, max(_time) AS last_seen BY src_ip
| convert ctime(first_seen) ctime(last_seen)


``` 2. Suspicious IP (MITRE T1110): any login attempt from the known-bad IP list in config.yml. ```
index=main sourcetype=auth_log
| rex "user=(?<user>\S+) \| ip=(?<src_ip>\S+) \| event=(?<event>\S+) \| status=(?<result>\S+) \| location=(?<city>[^,]+),(?<country>\S+)"
| search src_ip IN ("45.155.205.13", "185.220.101.4", "91.219.237.244")
| stats count AS attempts, values(user) AS users, values(result) AS results, min(_time) AS first_seen BY src_ip
| convert ctime(first_seen)


``` 3. Impossible travel (MITRE T1078): two successful logins by the same user from different countries
    within 30 minutes. This is simpler than detect_impossible_travel(), which also computes the haversine
    distance and required speed; here a country change inside the window is treated as the signal. ```
index=main sourcetype=auth_log
| rex "user=(?<user>\S+) \| ip=(?<src_ip>\S+) \| event=(?<event>\S+) \| status=(?<result>\S+) \| location=(?<city>[^,]+),(?<country>\S+)"
| search result=success
| sort 0 user _time
| streamstats current=f last(city) AS prev_city, last(country) AS prev_country, last(_time) AS prev_time BY user
| eval minutes_apart = round((_time - prev_time) / 60, 1)
| where isnotnull(prev_country) AND country != prev_country AND minutes_apart <= 30
| table _time user prev_city city minutes_apart src_ip
